---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import homeDark from '../../assets/home-dark.png';
            <p>
                <Image
                    src={homeDark}
                    alt="home page dark mode"
                    style="float: right; margin: 0 0 1em 2em; width: 300px; max-width: 40vw; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);"
                />
                This screenshot shows the home page of the app in dark mode. The app is designed to be simple and intuitive to use, with a focus on providing useful information about fossils and geology. You can explore different locations, view fossil records, and learn about the geological history of different areas. The app is still in development, so there may be some bugs and missing features, but I'm working hard to make it as useful and enjoyable as possible.
            </p>
            </p>
            <p>
                <img
                    srcset="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/home-dark.png&w=640 640w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/home-dark.png&w=1280 1280w, /.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/home-dark.png&w=2048 2048w"
                    sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
                    src="/.netlify/images?url=/src/assets/home-dark.png&w=640"
                    alt="home page dark mode"
                    style="float: right; margin: 0 0 1em 2em; width: 300px; max-width: 40vw; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);"
                />
                This screenshot shows the home page of the app in dark mode. The app is designed to be simple and intuitive to use, with a focus on providing useful
                information about fossils and geology. You can explore different locations, view fossil records, and learn about the geological history of different
                areas. The app is still in development, so there may be some bugs and missing features, but I'm working hard to make it as useful and enjoyable as
                possible.
            </p>
            <p>
                In this image you can see the main features of the home page, including the search bar at the top where you can enter a location to explore, and
                the various sections below that provide information about fossils, geology, and other related topics. You can click on different sections to
                learn more about specific topics, and there are also links to other pages where you can find more detailed information and resources.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
